    "rulesNotes": [
        "A Skaven warband must include a minimum of 3 models.",
        "A Skaven warband may contain a maximum of 20 models.",
        "The warband must include exactly one Assassin Adept.",
        "The warband may include a single Eshin Sorcerer.",
        "The warband may include up to two Black Skaven.",
        "The warband may include up to two Night Runners.",
        "The warband may include any number of Verminkin.",
        "The warband may include any number of Giant Rats.",
        "The warband may include a single Rat Ogre.",
        "Giant Rats and the Rat Ogre may never carry weapons or armour.",
        "Two Skaven-only equipment lists exist here: Heroes and Henchmen (Night Runners use the Henchmen list, per the source text). Throwing Stars and Club appear on the printed equipment lists but their rules text could not be reliably sourced, so they are left out here rather than guessed at.",
        "Skill-category access could not be read from the source PDF's table for this warband (checkmark glyphs did not survive extraction) - set here as a best-effort judgement call (Assassin Adept gets everything including the Special list; Black Skaven leans Combat/Strength; the Eshin Sorcerer leans Academic to suit spellcasting; the Night Runner leans Speed) - verify against the printed skill table before relying on it for a competitive game."
    ]
